{"kind":"artifact","text":"GitHub connector, inbound half, at exact clean head 2e7319805688d7432e394862aabc0ecb47e9648d on request/github-connector-observe. Four commits: the observe library, the read-only fetch adapter, admission clauses, and the command that wires them.\n\nThis artifact exists so the documentation describing this behaviour has something whose retirement would mean go and re-read the code. The docset anchor gate refused the page when it rested on the charter, correctly: a charter is a `propose`, and retiring a policy statement says nothing about whether a description of the implementation still holds.\n\nExercised against the live workroom rather than only in tests: it refused an absent charter, refused the retired first draft, appended nothing under the ratified charter while no clause existed, then observed generalbusiness-ai/gitseq#1 as aa31d08e once hugh stated clause 0bb7957c, and reported nothing new on a second run.","body":{"commit":"2e7319805688d7432e394862aabc0ecb47e9648d","path":"internal/connector"}}